<rml>
<head>
    <title>Lighting</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="scrim" id="lighting-scrim">
        <div class="case">

            <div class="lid stacked">
                <div class="lid-top">
                    <div class="head">
                        <div class="mark"></div>
                        <div class="title">Lighting</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chrome">
                        <div class="win-btn" id="modal-close"><svg class="win-ic" src="../icons/x.svg"/></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="hint">Every change shows at once. Up and down to move, left and right to change, Escape or the pad's B goes back</div>
            </div>

            <!-- Built from the lighting model (ui_lighting.cpp), the way the settings rows are: one
                 row per control, each with an Off where off makes sense and a scale of levels, and
                 a Reset row at the end that puts the design's values back. -->
            <div class="rows long" id="lighting-rows" data-model="rows"></div>

            <div class="foot">
                <span>Saved as you change it</span>
                <span id="lighting-foot">Each part switches on its own; the tools for inspecting a single pass are under Debugging</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
